From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_bcm: Keep the default address when none is
 given

When btbcm recognises a controller's default address, hci_bcm sets
HCI_QUIRK_USE_BDADDR_PROPERTY so that the boot loader can supply the
unit's address in local-bd-address. If the property is missing or still
the all-zero placeholder, the HCI core then leaves the controller
unconfigured, and Bluetooth stays off until userspace sets an address.

The iPad mini 1's BCM4334 reports Apple's placeholder 43:34:43:34:1F:AC,
which btbcm treats as a default, and its boot stage (the Cascadia loader)
passes no address. Its device tree used to carry a fixed address, shared
by every unit, to keep Bluetooth working; with a zero placeholder there
instead, keep the controller's default address and say so, rather than
leaving the controller unconfigured. An address from the boot loader is
still used as before.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
index 89d4c22..a6a0635 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
@@ -578,6 +578,17 @@ static int bcm_flush(struct hci_uart *hu)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* The same test hci_dev_get_bd_addr_from_property() applies. */
+static bool bcm_has_bdaddr_property(struct hci_dev *hdev)
+{
+	struct fwnode_handle *fwnode = dev_fwnode(hdev->dev.parent);
+	bdaddr_t ba;
+
+	return fwnode_property_read_u8_array(fwnode, "local-bd-address",
+					     (u8 *)&ba, sizeof(ba)) >= 0 &&
+	       bacmp(&ba, BDADDR_ANY);
+}
+
 static int bcm_setup(struct hci_uart *hu)
 {
 	struct bcm_data *bcm = hu->priv;
@@ -641,10 +652,17 @@ static int bcm_setup(struct hci_uart *hu)
 
 	/* Some devices ship with the controller default address.
 	 * Allow the bootloader to set a valid address through the
-	 * device tree.
+	 * device tree. When it has not, keep the default address
+	 * rather than leaving the controller unconfigured.
 	 */
-	if (test_bit(HCI_QUIRK_INVALID_BDADDR, &hu->hdev->quirks))
-		set_bit(HCI_QUIRK_USE_BDADDR_PROPERTY, &hu->hdev->quirks);
+	if (test_bit(HCI_QUIRK_INVALID_BDADDR, &hu->hdev->quirks)) {
+		if (bcm_has_bdaddr_property(hu->hdev)) {
+			set_bit(HCI_QUIRK_USE_BDADDR_PROPERTY, &hu->hdev->quirks);
+		} else {
+			bt_dev_warn(hu->hdev, "BCM: No device address given, keeping the default");
+			clear_bit(HCI_QUIRK_INVALID_BDADDR, &hu->hdev->quirks);
+		}
+	}
 
 	if (!bcm_request_irq(bcm))
 		err = bcm_setup_sleep(hu);
